{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עשק", :translit "esek", :gloss "contention/oppression"} {:he "כנגד בבל", :translit "keneged bavel", :gloss "corresponding to Babylon"} {:he "שעשקו את בית יהודה", :translit "she'asku et beit yehudah", :gloss "who oppressed the house of Judah"} {:he "ומיד עושקיהם כח", :translit "u'miyad oskim koach", :gloss "and immediately He oppresses them with strength"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-play: the place-name עשק is read as a foreshadowing of Babylon's oppression of Judah"}], :frame {:text "The name of the well that Isaac's servants dug, called עשק ('Esek,' meaning 'contention'), is read as an allusion to Babylon, the empire that oppressed the kingdom of Judah. The fall of Judah to Babylon is narrated in 2 Kings 25, and Babylon's identity as the oppressor is echoed in Zechariah 2:12 and Ezra 4:23.", :sources ["2 Kings 25" "Zechariah 2:12" "Ezra 4:23"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word-play: the place-name עשק is read as a foreshadowing of Babylon's oppression of Judah", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:20.703500985Z", :model "glm-5.2"}